    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gavin Sheets** (59.95) and **Tyler Freeman** (59.49) stand out as our highest-upside starters, effectively anchoring the lineup against vulnerable right-handed pitching. **Gavin Sheets** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Houser (4.60 xERA), with the platoon advantage and lineup position driving his scoring. Meanwhile, **Tyler Freeman** is a sneaky play due to extreme park factors (+14%) and a slow delivery from Peralta that heavily favors our strategy of hunting stolen bases; despite the tough matchup, his speed profile makes him an essential start. **Cal Raleigh** (74.55) remains the primary engine of our offense, as he finds himself in the strongest position of the day, leveraging an elite matchup against P\u00e9rez and a prime #2 spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board centered on **Lawrence Butler**, who squeezed into the starting rotation with a 51.42 score. While he faces the daunting task of opposing Wheeler (2.89 xERA), his score was propped up by a rare 13% boost from a favorable platoon split and an encouraging wind-out forecast at the venue, which gives him the highest ceiling of our \"marginal\" tier players. Conversely, **Daulton Varsho** was the closest player to cracking the starting lineup, ultimately hitting the bench due to a lack of confirmed status and a difficult matchup against McClanahan. Had **Daulton Varsho** been confirmed in the lineup, his profile as a speed threat would have likely vaulted him over **Jonathan Aranda** (47.02), whose score was suppressed by a negative platoon adjustment against Corbin. \n\nFinally, a note of caution for the day: **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (55.68) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (47.46) are facing elite arms in Ragans and Skenes, respectively. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an auto-start due to his pedigree and volume, the 19% SP skill penalty suggests our offensive expectations for the top of the order should be tempered. We are also monitoring **Jeremiah Jackson** closely; despite an unfavorable #9 spot in the order, his 100% stolen base potential against a slow pitcher keeps him in the lineup, though he represents one of our most volatile assets today. Ensure all rostered players like **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Wenceel Perez**, and **Drew Gilbert** remain monitored for defensive substitutions or late-breaking injury reports.",
